{"results":[{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"Q92008","uniProtkbId":"SHH_DANRE","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Sonic hedgehog protein"},"shortNames":[{"value":"SHHA"}],"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q62226"}],"value":"3.1.-.-"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q62226"}],"value":"Shh unprocessed N-terminal signaling and C-terminal autoprocessing domains"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q62226"}],"value":"ShhNC"}]},{"fullName":{"value":"VHH-1"}}],"contains":[{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"Sonic hedgehog protein A N-product"}},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q62226"}],"value":"Shh N-terminal processed signaling domains"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q62226"}],"value":"ShhNp"}]},{"fullName":{"value":"Sonic hedgehog protein N-product"},"shortNames":[{"value":"ShhN"}]}]}],"flag":"Precursor"},"genes":[{"geneName":{"value":"shha"},"synonyms":[{"value":"shh"},{"value":"vhh1"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q15465"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q62226"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12588855"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16452095"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"7583153"}],"value":"Together with shhb/twhh shares a redundant function in posterior specification of the anterior otic regions of the ear during development (PubMed:12588855). In conjunction with shhb/twhh, required for correct pre-thalamic development and thalamic development during embryogenesis, via downstream regulation of differentiation factors dbx1a, dlx2a and ptch1 (PubMed:16452095). The C-terminal part of the sonic hedgehog protein precursor displays an autoproteolysis and a cholesterol transferase activity (By similarity). Both activities result in the cleavage of the full-length protein into two parts (ShhN and ShhC) followed by the covalent attachment of a cholesterol moiety to the C-terminal of the newly generated ShhN (By similarity). Both activities occur in the endoplasmic reticulum (By similarity). Once cleaved, ShhC is degraded in the endoplasmic reticulum (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION","molecule":"Sonic hedgehog protein"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q15465"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q62226"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"7583153"}],"value":"The dually lipidated sonic hedgehog protein N-product (ShhNp) is a morphogen which is essential for a variety of patterning events during development (By similarity). Involved in dorso-ventral patterning of the brain and in early patterning of the developing eyes (PubMed:7583153). Binds to the patched (PTCH1) receptor, which functions in association with smoothened (SMO), to activate the transcription of target genes (By similarity). In the absence of SHH, PTCH1 represses the constitutive signaling activity of SMO (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION","molecule":"Sonic hedgehog protein A N-product"}],"features":[],"uniProtKBCrossReferences":[{"database":"ZFIN","id":"ZDB-GENE-980526-166","properties":[{"key":"GeneName","value":"shha"}]}],"sequence":{"value":"","length":418,"molWeight":46403,"crc64":"CF000AFFFD2F5795","md5":"6AD3955FF60C6EE689FF61F055797F92"},"extraAttributes":{"uniParcId":"UPI000013593E"}},
